# Never Edit Generated or Vendored Files

Edits to build output and dependencies are lost on the next build or install, and they
silently diverge from source. Always change the source file, then rebuild.

## Off-limits paths

Never create, edit, or delete files under:

- `node_modules/**` (including workspace symlinks such as `node_modules/@repo/*`)
- `**/dist/**`, `**/build/**`, `**/out/**`
- `apps/web/.next/**`, `apps/web/.open-next/**`, `apps/web/.wrangler*/**`
- `apps/agent/.mastra/output/**`
- `.turbo/**`, `**/.turbo/**`

Reading these files is fine — use them for debugging, stack traces, and checking
third-party APIs.

## Map output back to source

| You landed in | Edit instead |
|---------------|--------------|
| `packages/<pkg>/dist/index.js` | `packages/<pkg>/src/**` |
| `node_modules/@repo/<pkg>/**` | `packages/<pkg>/src/**` (it is a pnpm symlink) |
| `apps/agent/.mastra/output/**` | `apps/agent/src/mastra/**` |
| `apps/web/.next/**` | `apps/web/app/**`, `apps/web/features/**`, `apps/web/components/**` |

```
❌ Edit apps/agent/.mastra/output/index.mjs to fix a tool description
✅ Edit apps/agent/src/mastra/tools/booking/create-booking.ts, then rebuild
```

## Third-party packages

A bug in a `node_modules` package is never fixed by patching it in place. Work around it
in our own code, upgrade the dependency, or tell the user a patch (e.g. `pnpm patch`) is
needed — and let them decide.
